2. Pressure of blood flow: As blood flows more slowly due to increased viscosity, the pressure in the cardiovascular system increases. This is because the blood is trying to overcome the higher resistance in the blood vessels, leading to a rise in pressure to maintain the same flow rate. This can cause the circulatory system to work less efficiently and may lead to symptoms such as shortness of breath, shortness of breath, and shortness of breath.

