","The expression of oncogenes contributes to tumor growth by promoting uncontrolled cell division and survival. These genes, which are often mutated or mutated versions of normal cellular genes called proto-oncogenes, can be compared to cancer-causing agents. They disrupt the normal cell cycle and promote the development of malignant tumors.

The main ways oncogenes contribute to tumor growth include:

