The standard enthalpy change for this reaction (ΔH°) can be calculated using the following equation:

ΔH° = ΔHf(FeCl4]2- - [ΔHf(Fe(H2O)6]2+ + 2ΔHf(Cl-)]

where ΔHf represents the enthalpy of formation for each species.

We are given the following values:

