2. Charge transport: The electronic structure of GO allows it to facilitate the transport of photogenerated electrons from the TiO2 nanoparticles to the external circuit. This improved charge transport can lead to an increase in the overall efficiency of the solar cell. However, if the ratio of GO to TiO2 is too high, the increased resistance of the GO can hinder the charge transport process, leading to a decrease in the overall efficiency of the solar cell.

