   \[
   \text{S} + \text{O}_2 \rightarrow \text{SO}_2
   \]
   From the equation, 1 mole of S reacts with 1 mole of O₂.
   Molar mass of S = 32 g/mol, Molar mass of O₂ = 32 g/mol.
   \[
   \text{Weight of S} = \frac{57.5 \text{ g}}{32 \text{ g/mol}} \times 32 \text{ g/mol} = 57.5 \text{ g}
   \]

