2. **Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) Spectroscopy:** If the chiral alcohol has a diastereotopic proton (protons in the same molecule but with different chemical environments), the NMR spectrum will show two distinct signals for these protons. By comparing the chemical shifts and coupling constants of these signals to those of known enantiomers, the configuration of the product can be determined.

