- \( n - 1 \) is the number of comparisons for partitioning the list.
- \( 2C\left(\frac{n}{2}\right) \) accounts for the comparisons needed to sort the two sublists of size \( \frac{n}{2} \).

This recurrence relation describes the best-case behavior of QuickSort when the pivot always divides the list into two equal parts. 

Final Answer: The recurrence relation is \(\boxed{C(n) = (n - 1) + 2C\left(\frac{n}{2}\right)}\).
