#### Solution:  
1. **Mass of the part**: \( m = 1.2 \, \text{kg} \).  
2. **Density of the part**: \( \rho = 7150 \, \text{kg/m}^3 \).  
3. **Surface area of the part**: \( A = 0.075 \, \text{m}^2 \).  
4. **Thermal conductivity of the material**: \( k = 95 \, \text{W/mK} \).  
5. **Specific heat of the material**: \( c_p = 385 \, \text{J/kg K} \).  
6. **Initial temperature of the part**: \( T_0 = 345^\circ \text{C} \).  
7. **Ambient temperature**: \( T_a = 20^\circ \text{C} \).  
8. **Convective heat transfer coefficient**: \( h = 56.8 \, \text{W/m}^2 \text{K} \).  

#### (i) Temperature after 5 minutes:  
The temperature of the part after 5 minutes can be calculated using the lumped parameter method:  
\[
T(t) = T_a + (T_0 - T_a) e^{-h A t / (m c_p)}
\]  
Substituting the given values:  
\[
T(5) = 20 + (345 - 20) e^{-56.8 \times 0.075 \times 5 / (1.2 \times 385)} = 20 + (325) e^{-0.092} = 20 + 280.6 = 300.6^\circ \text{C}
\]  

#### (ii) Time required to reach 50°C:  
To find the time required to reach 50°C, we rearrange the lumped parameter equation:  
\[
t = \frac{m c_p}{h A} \ln \left( \frac{T_0 - T_a}{T(t) - T_a} \right)
\]  
Substituting the given values:  
\[
t = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{56.8 \times 0.075} \ln \left( \frac{345 - 20}{50 - 20} \right) = 10.2 \ln(2.8) = 10.2 \times 1.08 = 10.99 \, \text{hr}
\]  

#### (iii) Time constant:  
The time constant \( \tau \) is given by:  
\[
\tau = \frac{m c_p}{h A} = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{56.8 \times 0.075} = 10.2 \, \text{hr}
