   \[
   \varepsilon_1 = \frac{\varepsilon_x + \varepsilon_y}{2} + \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{(\varepsilon_x - \varepsilon_y)^2 + \gamma_{xy}^2}
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   \[
   \varepsilon_1 = \frac{-0.0005 + 0.0035}{2} + \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{(-0.0005 - 0.0035)^2 + (0.003)^2}
   \]
   \[
   \varepsilon_1 = \frac{0.002}{2} + \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{(-0.004)^2 + (0.003)^2}
   \]
   \[
   \varepsilon_1 = 0.001 + \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{0.00016 + 0.00009}
   \]
   \[
   \varepsilon_1 = 0.001 + \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{0.00025}
   \]
   \[
