     \[
     E = \frac{(1000 \times 1.0 - 1.0 \times 1.0)}{(1 - 1.4)} = -300 \text{ bar L}
     \]
     Convert bar L to joules:
     \[
     E = -300 \times 10^5 \text{ J}
     \]
     (Note: The negative sign indicates energy release.)

2. **Calculate the total energy of the HMTD explosion:**
   - The energy in the pressure wave is 70% of the total energy:
     \[
     E_{\text{total}} = \frac{E}{0.7} = \frac{-300 \times 10^5}{-0.7} = 425 \times 10^5 \text{ J}
     \]

3. **Calculate the mass of TNT required:**
   - The energy per gram of TNT is 4680 J/g:
     \[
     \text{Mass of TNT} = \frac{E_{\text{total}}}{4680} = \frac{425 \times 10^5}{4680} \approx 87.0 \text{ g}
     \]

