   The percentage change in the rate of heat transfer is:  
   \[
   \text{Percentage Change} = \left( \frac{2 \times 168 - 168}{168} \right) \times 100 = 100\%
   \]  

   **Final Answer:**  
   The rate of heat transfer increases by \(\boxed{100\%}\).
